# Secrets and local runtime data. .gitignore is the source of truth for what must never be
# published; COPY . . in the build stage will otherwise pull these into a layer, and once this
# image builds in CI with layer caching, "local only" stops being true.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a .dockerignore pattern with no slash matches only the context root, not
# every directory -- so these need the same **/ prefix already used above for node_modules and
# dist, or an apps/server/.env.local slips straight through COPY . .
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
